obo:GO_0000723  a  owl:Class .

:R-HSA-171306  a            obo:GO_0000723 , owl:NamedIndividual ;
        rdfs:comment        "Multiple steps, including C-strand resection, telomerase-mediated elongation, and C-strand synthesis are involved in processing and maintaining the telomere. Though this module posits a linear transit for the steps, in humans it is not well understood how these steps are coordinated and what other events may be involved.<br><br>Telomeric DNA can form higher order structures. Electron microscopy of telomeric DNA isolated from human cells provided evidence for lariat-type structures termed telomeric loops, or t-loops (Griffith et al., 1999). t-loops are proposed to result from the invasion of the 3' G-rich single strand overhang into the double stranded telomeric TTAGGG repeat tract. The function of the t-loop is presumed to be the masking of the 3' telomeric overhang. Multiple protein factors can bind telomeric DNA and likely contribute to dynamic, higher order structures." ;
        rdfs:label          "Packaging Of Telomere Ends" ;
        dc:contributor      "Authored: Blackburn, EH, Seidel, J, 2006-03-09 19:41:08" , "Reviewed: Hayashi, Makoto T, 2020-04-29" , "GOC:reactome_curators" , "Reviewed: Price, C, 2006-07-13 18:33:38" , "Edited: Orlic-Milacic, Marija, 2020-05-04" ;
        dc:date             "2023-06-21" ;
        pav:providedBy      "https://reactome.org" ;
        oboInOwl:hasDbXref  "R-HSA-171306" ;
        skos:narrower       <http://model.geneontology.org/R-HSA-157579/R-HSA-157579> ;
        skos:note           "org.biopax.paxtools.model.level3.Pathway" .

